We are choosing between Datadog, Grafana Cloud, and a self-hosted stack (Prometheus, Loki and Grafana on our own Kubernetes).

## Comparison table
table = Option,Setup effort,Alerting,Log search,Lock-in,Annual cost; Datadog,Low,Excellent,Excellent,High,"$412,000"; Grafana Cloud,Low,Good,Good,Medium,"$236,000"; Self-hosted,High,Good,Fair,Low,"$148,000 + 1.5 engineers"

## Three-year cost
data cumulative = year,Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted incl. staff; 2027,412,865,418; 2028,865,496,706; 2029,1363,782,1004
data cumulative3 = year,Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted incl. staff; 2027,412,236,418; 2028,865,496,706; 2029,1363,782,1004
chart line cumulative3 x=year unit=k$ focus=Grafana Cloud title="Cumulative cost, thousands of dollars"

Grafana Cloud stays cheapest in every year once self-hosted staff time is counted: $782k over three years against $1,004k self-hosted and $1,363k for Datadog.

## Pros and cons
### Datadog
- Pro: low setup effort
- Pro: excellent alerting and log search
- Con: highest cost by far
- Con: high lock-in
### Grafana Cloud
- Pro: low setup effort
- Pro: dashboards stay portable
- Con: log search is good, not excellent
### Self-hosted
- Pro: lowest license cost and lock-in
- Con: high setup effort
- Con: needs 1.5 more engineers
- Con: fair log search

## Recommendation
! **Choose Grafana Cloud.** It is the cheapest option once staff time is counted, and it keeps our dashboards portable.

! The Datadog quote expires on 2026-11-30. The self-hosted figures assume we can hire 1.5 engineers, which is not yet approved.
